<blockquote>
<p>Its blades consist of a single piece of unknown polymer material similar to plastic</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Two problems with this; firstly, it should be 'an unknown polymer'.</p>
<p>Secondly: similar to plastic? If one is being scientific enough to use the term polymer, surely one would give a specific type of plastic rather than simply saying 'plastic'. It also seems a little unnecessary to make this material so mysterious, why not just define it?</p>
<p>Furthermore, I'm not sure you can have an unknown polymer. You take a sample, look at it, name it and now you have a new polymer that is now known. You could say an unencountered polymer but it can never remain unknown unless something is stopping the Foundation from taking a sample.</p>

